    "perplexity": {
      "description": "The A&M Albums by Dodgy is a 4LP box set issued by Demon Records that gathers the band’s classic 1990s A&M-era studio albums: The Dodgy Album, Homegrown, and Free Peace Sweet. It was presented as the first dedicated vinyl box set for this period, with the albums newly reissued on 180g coloured vinyl and Free Peace Sweet expanded with the bonus tracks “Grateful Moon” and “Is It Me?” from its initial limited pressing.\n\nThe set captures Dodgy at the heart of their melodic rock/pop sound, moving from the bright, guitar-driven indie-pop of their 1993 debut to the more polished, hook-heavy songwriting that brought them wider recognition on Homegrown and Free Peace Sweet. The Dodgy Album introduced the group’s distinctive blend of chiming guitars and catchy choruses, while Homegrown and Free Peace Sweet refined that formula into the more confident, radio-friendly style that defined their mid-1990s peak.\n\nFor collectors, the box set is significant because it restores these albums to vinyl together for the first time in this form, and it presents Dodgy’s A&M years as a cohesive snapshot of a band that helped define a lighter, melodic strand of British rock in the 1990s. The compilation format also highlights the band’s progression across their most commercially visible era, making it both a convenient overview and a substantial archival release.",
